    "physical_description": "Man's square headdress of tie-and-dye and wax-resist (Batik) cotton. The centre is dyed green and purple by the tie-and-dye (kain kembangan) process, and the borders of the inner square and of the four sides are drawn by hand and dyed by the wax-resist method in brown and blue on a buff coloured ground.\n\nIn the centre is a square 'modang' in green bordered with Batik-work of repeated small floral motives, mottling and in-turned spikes. The field outside this centre is of dark purple, and without ornament. The Batik-work outer borders have each a wide band of undulating stems of flowers and leaves between narrow fillets of repeated small floral and geometrical patterns. Small details of the border are in the white of the undyed ground.",
